WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.450
From the strange side effects of long-distance
relationships that wind up going fully multiversal

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:10.400
to the challenges of a super-soldier serum
glow-up, here are some pretty weird things

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.800
about Captain America and Peggy Carter's relationship.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.720
We might as well start by acknowledging that
even in its most basic form, Steve Rogers

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.740
and Peggy Carter's relationship is definitely
weird when you compare it to traditional love

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:24.990
stories.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:28.810
From Peggy's point of view, it involves a
man who dies and then comes back 70 years

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.150
later looking exactly as handsome as he did
in 1941.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:37.830
The decades in the middle were occupied by
a long and successful career as a spy, not

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:43.140
to mention a marriage to someone else and
two kids that we never even learn about.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.390
From Steve's point of view, it's even weirder.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:49.800
As far as he's concerned, he goes to what
he thinks is his death, only to wake up a

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.990
few seconds later to find that everything,
including Peggy, has moved on into the next

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:55.430
century without him.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:59.370
He goes immediately from promising to take
her dancing to hanging out with her as she's

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:03.490
dying of old age after a long life that he
wasn't really a part of.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:08.420
Then, he goes back in time to put a ring on
it after seeing her on her literal deathbed.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.460
He was at her funeral before he was at their
wedding.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.060
That's not usually the right order for those,
unless something has gone terribly wrong.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.120
And then we get into the really weird stuff.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.800
If we're going to get the weirdest and most
obvious sticking point about Steve and Peggy's

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:27.030
relationship out of the way right up front,
we're going to have to to talk about Sharon

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:28.030
Carter.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:31.320
It's pretty clear from the way that the movies
unfold that the relationship between Steve

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.750
and Peggy wasn't originally intended to be
the endgame, so to speak.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:40.130
Captain America has famously been characterized
since his return to the comics in the 1960s

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:41.830
as a man out of time.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:45.729
He's the iconic hero from the country's past
who returns like King Arthur at our moment

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:46.979
of greatest need.

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:49.080
"I understood that reference."

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:53.300
The thing is, nobody actually wants a superhero
who needs Peter Parker to explain how to use

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:59.380
his iPhone, so Cap is also a guy who acclimates
very quickly to new situations, whether he's

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:04.160
fighting bad guys or catching up on 70 years
of missed pop culture.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.560
Losing the years he would've spent with Peggy
is a necessary ingredient for giving his time

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.640
on ice some emotional weight.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.730
Waking up in the 21st century isn't that much
of a tragedy, he even talks about how much

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:19.390
he prefers present-day food to whatever he
was snacking on back in the '40s, so the only

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:22.450
thing that he really loses is Peggy.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:25.620
Even that turns out to only be a tragedy for
Steve.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.650
In Winter Soldier, we see him as he watches
Peggy explain that after the war, she got

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:35.170
married to an unnamed soldier and had a very
happy and fulfilling life working for S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:39.340
As Steve's story continues, the loss of his
relationship with Peggy. and eventually the

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:44.400
loss of Peggy herself, becomes the one big
tragedy of Captain America's history, especially

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:49.440
once the other close companion he lost makes
his own miraculous return from the dead.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.360
That also means it's something he can move
past, which, of course, he does...right into

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.800
the waiting arms of Sharon Carter.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.720
And that is a problem.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:02.040
As much as we all might love Steve and Peggy
together, there's a pretty good reason why

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:07.890
Sharon shows up in The Winter Soldier to add
another side to this cross-time love triangle.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:12.599
In the Captain America comics, Sharon is Cap's
longest tenured love interest.

00:03:12.599 --> 00:03:16.040
She even predates any of Steve's other love
interests, including Peggy.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:21.230
In fact, until she popped up on the big screen
in 2011, Peggy was actually a pretty minor

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.710
character who mostly appeared in flashbacks.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:29.379
Sharon, on the other hand, was the long-time
on-again, off-again romance that always seemed

00:03:29.379 --> 00:03:32.730
like the default setting for Captain America's
love life.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:36.050
After all, if you're going to have Steve Rogers
continue his adventures in the present day

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:40.860
after spending 70 years trapped in an iceberg,
he should probably have a present-day love

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:41.940
interest.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.260
The First Avenger was framed as a flashback,
so Sharon was held back from the Marvel Cinematic

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:49.069
Universe until the second film.

00:03:49.069 --> 00:03:52.980
Since there was already a character in the
comics who could provide a connection to Cap,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.319
Peggy got the role of the bittersweet, tragic
romance in the first movie.

00:03:57.319 --> 00:04:00.980
Unfortunately for Sharon, it turned out to
be a little too bitter for everyone who wanted

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:06.800
a happy ending, so Cap never really got over
Peggy...which created a whole other problem.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:12.000
This all brings us to the really weird thing
about the Cap-Peggy-Sharon triangle.

00:04:12.019 --> 00:04:16.260
Even if they're both age-appropriate due to
some suspended animation hijinx, it's usually

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:20.549
frowned upon to date your ex-girlfriend's
niece, especially if she's about 50 years

00:04:20.549 --> 00:04:21.639
younger.

00:04:21.639 --> 00:04:25.379
And then there's the problem that we get into
with all the time travel that comes at the

00:04:25.379 --> 00:04:26.779
end of Endgame.

00:04:26.779 --> 00:04:30.650
It's all well and good that Cap's reward for
saving the universe is that he gets to go

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:36.120
back and be reunited with his one true love,
but Sharon is Peggy's niece.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:39.699
Steve and Peggy get married, and if you look
closely you can spot a wedding ring, then

00:04:39.699 --> 00:04:42.580
Sharon is also Steve's niece.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:46.400
Which means Captain America straight-up made
out with his own niece like two days after

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.719
his wife's funeral.

00:04:47.719 --> 00:04:52.460
Sure, Sharon wasn't his niece yet, and Peggy
wasn't his wife before she died, which is

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:57.780
a pretty concise explanation of the headaches
that result from time travel, but still.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:02.240
You can use all the Ancient One's magic timeline
graphs you want to explain why it's actually

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:06.830
okay for all of this to happen, but even the
most die-hard fan of the Steve and Peggy romance

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:11.129
has to admit that it's weird that Captain
America's dating pool never really extends

00:05:11.129 --> 00:05:12.640
beyond his own family.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:16.720
One of the really sweet things about Cap and
Peggy's relationship is that the two characters

00:05:16.759 --> 00:05:21.189
always carry pictures of each other, even
when they're separated by the gulfs of time.

00:05:21.189 --> 00:05:23.440
Cap has his picture of Peggy that he clipped
out of the newspaper.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:27.949
When we get a glimpse of her desk in the '70s
during Endgame, we see that Peggy keeps a

00:05:27.949 --> 00:05:32.919
framed photo of Steve, even 30 years after
his presumed death in the Arctic.

00:05:32.919 --> 00:05:34.550
What makes it even sweeter?

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:38.880
It's a photo of Steve before his transformation
from the Super Soldier Serum, showing us that

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.360
she loves him for who he is on the inside,
and not just because mad science turned him

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.999
into the Marvel Universe's hunkiest possible
Chris.

00:05:46.999 --> 00:05:50.629
At the same time, that's a little unusual
on its own right, isn't it?

00:05:50.629 --> 00:05:54.009
Steve had to have been Captain America for
at least a few years, right?

00:05:54.009 --> 00:05:58.910
The First Avenger opens with the Red Skull
discovering the Tesseract in 1941, and it's

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:03.599
implied that the end of the movie happens
close to, or even immediately before, V-E

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.280
Day on May 8th, 1945.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:10.469
Even if you give him plenty of time to catch
up on the news, volunteer, and go through

00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:15.610
training, that's still two or three years
where he's the hunk that we all know and love.

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:19.589
Judging by the increasing tightness of his
shirts over the course of the MCU, it seems

00:06:19.589 --> 00:06:23.939
clear that Steve himself is pretty comfortable
with his ridiculously shredded new body.

00:06:23.939 --> 00:06:26.580
"That is America's ass."

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:30.699
There isn't a big question of who Steve's
"true self" is like you might see with Superman

00:06:30.699 --> 00:06:31.909
and Clark Kent.

00:06:31.909 --> 00:06:35.400
If that's the case, then maybe Peggy's photo
isn't really for Steve at all.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:38.120
Maybe it's just a tribute to how much she
loves symbolism.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:43.280
Even at the best of times, relatively speaking,
Captain America and Peggy Carter's relationship

00:06:43.289 --> 00:06:44.430
wasn't easy.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:47.050
Of course, it had to be at least a little
rocky.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:50.749
That's where the drama comes in, and while
it might just be nice to watch two people

00:06:50.749 --> 00:06:55.659
have a perfectly content relationship while
also destroying sci-fi pseudo-Nazis, even

00:06:55.659 --> 00:06:58.300
romantic stories are driven by conflict.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:02.789
Still, most traditional romances don't involve
one party shooting at the other with a handgun

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:04.169
four times.

00:07:04.169 --> 00:07:08.159
When she catches Cap in a superheroic makeout
session with a fellow intelligence officer

00:07:08.159 --> 00:07:13.009
played by Natalie Dormer, Peggy is incensed,
even though she and Steve are definitely not

00:07:13.009 --> 00:07:14.620
a couple yet.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.340
Steve's not blameless here, either.

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:20.270
He immediately gets defensive and goes way
too far in response, implying that she's getting

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.279
some action from Howard Stark.

00:07:22.279 --> 00:07:23.960
It's a bad scene all over.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:28.669
It all comes to a head once Stark himself
shows up and, oblivious to this little tiff,

00:07:28.669 --> 00:07:32.749
gives Cap a prototype of his famous shield,
and Peggy unloads four rounds at him, which

00:07:32.749 --> 00:07:36.259
is the kind of situation where it's okay to
be defensive, especially if you're holding

00:07:36.259 --> 00:07:38.080
a bulletproof shield.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:42.020
That brings the fight to an end, but is it
really a healthy foundation on which to build

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.620
a life together as romantic partners?

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:48.969
Is every argument that these two have in their
relationship going to end up involving firearms

00:07:48.969 --> 00:07:49.960
and vibranium?

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.200
"I could do this all day."

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:58.160
The question of how the alternate timelines
shake out if Captain America goes back to

00:07:58.169 --> 00:08:02.959
live a happy life with Peggy Carter is going
to prompt a whole lot of headaches, especially

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:06.200
if you try to make it line up with what we
see in Agent Carter.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:10.200
Steve's plane goes down somewhere before May
of 1945.

00:08:10.219 --> 00:08:15.159
Agent Carter's two seasons take place in 1946
and 1947.

00:08:15.159 --> 00:08:19.770
That gives us a couple of options as to what
might happen when Steve travels back in time.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:23.879
Let's say he goes back to shortly after he
vanished and gets that dance, which means

00:08:23.879 --> 00:08:27.389
that the events of Agent Carter don't happen
as we saw them.

00:08:27.389 --> 00:08:31.879
That could mean that Steve tags along as Peggy's
super-soldier sidekick, which would actually

00:08:31.879 --> 00:08:33.190
be pretty charming.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:37.130
Or maybe they wind up doing something else,
and there's no one around to stop Dottie Underwood

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:39.820
from murdering Howard Stark in the '40s.

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:44.120
That means Tony Stark is never born, which
means that this particular timeline probably

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:48.380
ends with Thanos destroying the Earth because
Hawkeye tried to fight him all by himself.

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:50.830
Want to get really weird with it?

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:55.220
Let's assume that after he departs for the
1940s, Steve settles in for a happy married

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:59.890
life and spends the next 70 years with Peggy
before arriving back on that park bench as

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:02.300
the world's most handsome hundred year old.

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:05.740
He might be back where he would've been without
being frozen in the ice, but he's still a

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:08.770
man out of time, just in the opposite direction.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:09.770
He's been to the future.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:10.770
And Peggy's a spy.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:15.320
There is no possible way that Peggy Carter
doesn't use Steve as a resource for information

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:20.410
on what's going to happen so that she can
more effectively do her job for S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:24.020
Even if Steve never got around to getting
the specifics, we know that he's at least

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:29.500
aware of a few pretty important things that
happened between 1945 and 2011, because we

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:32.200
see him writing them down in his little notebook.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:36.870
He knows that the moon landing happens in
1969, which is a pretty big deal!

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:38.240
He knows about the Berlin Wall!

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:42.690
He even knows that Apple Computers is a pretty
good investment when it goes public in 1980,

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:47.320
and all of that is just what we know from
seeing that single page in his notebook.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:51.910
But sure, maybe Captain America decides that
preserving as much of the timeline as possible

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:55.950
is worth not telling his wife things that
would help her prevent countless tragedies.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:57.210
He still knows that S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:09:57.210 --> 00:10:01.430
itself has been infiltrated by Hydra, and
that his best friend is alive in Russia, being

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:06.950
brainwashed into becoming a cyborg assassin
who kills Peggy's pal, Howard Stark.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:10.720
There's no way that Captain America and Agent
Carter don't at least try to deal with those

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:15.970
things, meaning that they're running the risk
of creating a very different timeline.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:19.740
On the other hand, Peggy would probably get
to try Thai food way earlier than she would've

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.650
otherwise, so that's nice.

